Earlier versions
  Versions up to and including 1.6.2 were published under the MIT License.
  Copies of those versions that people already have stay under the MIT
  License, which requires keeping the Owner's copyright notice in every copy.
  This License covers version 1.6.3 and every later version.

1. What everyone may do
  a. Play: download, build, install and run the Software on your own devices,
     and record, stream and share videos and screenshots of it (monetized or
     not), as long as you do not present the Software as made by anyone other
     than the Owner.
  b. Make content: create mods, charts, songs, scripts, characters, stages and
     other content that runs in the Software, and share it however you like.
     Your content is yours, as long as it does not contain the Software's
     code.
  c. Read the source code and learn from it.

2. Collaborators
  Anyone who wants to use the Software's code is welcome to, as a
  Collaborator. You become a Collaborator by forking the official repository
  on GitHub, and as one you may:
  a. change, build, run and test the Software in your fork;
  b. keep your fork on GitHub, as a fork of the official repository, with
     this License, the copyright notice and the credits unchanged;
  c. send your changes to the official repository (pull requests, patches,
     issues) and work on the Software with the Owner and the other
     Collaborators.
  A fork is a place to work on God's Hand, not a separate project: its
  README must say that it is a fork of "God's Hand of Principality and
  Demise by deatuamae67-crypto", with a link to the official repository.

3. Blatant copies are not allowed
  Unless the Owner has given written permission (section 4), nobody, a
  Collaborator included, may:
  a. publish, share or distribute builds of the Software or of a modified
     version of it, other than the official releases;
  b. publish its source code, or a modified version of it, anywhere other
     than the official repository and Collaborators' forks on GitHub;
  c. publish the Software, a modified version of it, or a program built from
     its code as a separate project or engine, under any name;
  d. remove or change the copyright notice, this License or the credits,
     present the Software or any part of it as their own work, or name
     themselves as its author or co-author;
  e. sell the Software or a modified version of it, or charge for access to
     either;
  f. use the names "God's Hand of Principality and Demise" or "God's Hand"
     for another project, other than to say that it is based on the Software.

4. Written permission
  The Owner can allow more in writing (for example, builds or releases of a
  fork under its own name) in an issue, discussion or pull request of the
  official repository, or in a file there. A permission covers only what it
  says, and the work must always credit the Software as "Based on God's Hand
  of Principality and Demise by deatuamae67-crypto", with a link to the
  official repository.

5. Contributions
  When you send a contribution to the official repository (a pull request, a
  patch, or code in an issue), you agree that the Owner may include it in the
  Software and publish it under this License or any later license the Owner
  chooses. You keep the copyright of your contribution and stay credited as
  its author in the repository's history.

6. Mods and mod packs
  The mod packs published on the "mods" release are not part of the Software
  and are not covered by this License. Not all of them are the Owner's: some
  were made by the Owner, and the others belong to their original creators,
  who keep every right to them. They are shared so they can be played in
  God's Hand.

7. Third-party parts
  These parts keep their own licenses, and nothing in this License limits
  what those licenses allow for them:
  - raylib (fetched at build time): zlib/libpng license,
    Copyright (c) 2013-2024 Ramon Santamaria
  - Lua 5.4: MIT license, Copyright (C) 1994-2024 Lua.org, PUC-Rio
  - miniz: MIT license, Copyright 2013-2014 RAD Game Tools and Valve Software
  - pl_mpeg: MIT license, Copyright Dominic Szablewski
  - The GLSL of JS Engine's screen effects in src/effects.cpp, taken from
    the Shaders.hx file of JS Engine
    (https://github.com/JordanSantiagoYT/FNF-JS-Engine): Apache License 2.0,
    see licenses/Apache-2.0.txt
  - The base game's character offsets and stage layouts in src/basegame.cpp,
    which follow Friday Night Funkin' (The Funkin' Crew): Apache License 2.0,
    see licenses/Apache-2.0.txt
  - assets/fonts/CinzelDecorative-Bold.ttf and assets/fonts/Rajdhani-Bold.ttf:
    SIL Open Font License 1.1 (see the OFL files next to them)
  Features from PulseForge, also by the Owner, were rewritten for this code
  base and are part of the Software.

